IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgn-nominees`

-- Traces for the regulative rules of sgn-nominees.l4 (generated by work/gen_rule_tests.py; the days are typed from the text, and the trace clock starts at 0).
-- A time-limited rule is FULFILLED when the act is done on the last day and BREACHED when it is done the next day; "on that date" is 0 days.
-- A rule with no time limit (keep a register) cannot be breached by lateness; it is listed under "Rules with no breach path (sgn)" in NOTES.md.

`s 386AKA test company` MEANS Company "Acme Pte Ltd"
`s 386AL test director` MEANS Director "D"
`s 386ALA test company` MEANS Company "Acme Pte Ltd"
`s 386ALB test shareholder` MEANS Individual "S"

-- 386AKA(1)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 386AKA(1) a company or foreign company must keep a register of nominee directors` `s 386AKA test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AKA test company` DOES `s 386AKA(1) keep a register of its directors who are nominees in the prescribed form and at the prescribed place` AT 3
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 386AKA(1) a company or foreign company must keep a register of nominee directors` `s 386AKA test company` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- 386AKA(2)
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 386AKA(2) a company or foreign company must not disclose the register of nominee directors to a member of the public` `s 386AKA test company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 386AKA test company` DOES `s 386AKA(2) disclose the register of nominee directors or any particulars in it, or make it available for inspection, to a member of the public` AT 9
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 386AKA(2) a company or foreign company must not disclose the register of nominee directors to a member of the public` `s 386AKA test company` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

